    ///which point the layers are the defaults the load produced and the view has not been handed its
    ///controls yet, because the view is created by the render *after* this. So the save wrote defaults
    ///over the very session being read, and the state only survived because it was already in hand: the
    ///page looked right and the store no longer was, so the reopen after that one lost it.
    ///
    ///Cleared in <see cref="applyRestoredSettings"/>, which is the render where the last of it lands.
    ///</summary>
    private bool restoringState = false;

    ///<summary>
    ///The layer names in force, as the CSV a layermap holds. Kept here so opening a file can apply them
    ///without a storage round trip on the path that draws.
    ///</summary>
    private string layerNames = "";

    ///<summary>
    ///Whether the Examples popup is up. Not saved into a session: it is a thing being done rather than a
    ///setting, and coming back to a dialog nobody left open would be a surprise.
    ///</summary>
    private bool showExamples = false;

    ///<summary>
    ///The thumbnail beside the example picker: the open file's shapes, and a viewBox framing them.
    ///
    ///Built when a file is opened rather than on each render, because building it is a flatten and a pass
